* Euclid's algorithm for the greatest common divisor, with To for the loop.
* The remainder of a divided by b is a - b·ip(a/b).
1.1 Set r = a - b·ip(a/b).
1.2 Set a = b.
1.3 Set b = r.
1.4 To step 1.1 if b ≠ 0.

2.1 Set a = u.
2.2 Set b = v.
2.3 Do part 1.
2.4 Type u, v, a in form 1.
Form 1:
The greatest common divisor of _____ and _____ is ____.

Set u = 1071.
Do part 2 for v = 462, 1029, 1000.
The greatest common divisor of  1071 and   462 is   21.
The greatest common divisor of  1071 and  1029 is   21.
The greatest common divisor of  1071 and  1000 is    1.
